US-031 is implemented and every quality gate passes on Linux and Windows, but graphics and mesh PSOs are not built, which the story arguably needed. I set `passes: true` on the strength of the acceptance criteria as written, so you may want to reconsider that.

**What's in place** (new `engine/shader/` library, `docs/shader-pipeline.md`)
- **Compile:** one HLSL source compiles to DXIL and SPIR-V with the pinned DXC that the build stages. Diagnostics come out as compiler-style text and as an `engine.shader_diagnostics` JSON report, from one list.
- **Reflection:** both targets are read from DXC's own listings into one binding model. Bindings are checked against the declared layouts, CPU struct offsets against the shader, and DXIL against SPIR-V.
- **Cache:** keys cover the request (source, includes, defines, entry, profile, target) and an environment (compiler fingerprint, backend, adapter). Edited includes are misses. A cache file from another environment is rejected, never merged.
- **Reload:** `ShaderProgram::reload` swaps to the new pipeline only after it exists. A compile, layout, or pipeline-creation failure keeps the last valid pipeline current.

**Verification**
- Linux: `ValidateVendor`, `linux-dev`, `linux-debug`, `linux-unit` (22/22), GCC equivalents (22/22), and ASan/UBSan `linux-sanitize` (22/22). Zero warnings.
- Windows: `ValidateVendor`, `win-dev`, `win-debug` (zero `warning C`), `win-unit` (21/21).
- RTX 5080, debug layers on: `--suite gpu --backend dx12` (14 cases) and `--suite gpu --backend vulkan` (15 cases) pass. The new GPU test builds the shader through `ShaderProgram`, dispatches it, and confirms the pipeline still runs after a failed reload.
- Not run: GitHub CI (not pushed), Linux GPU suites (no Vulkan device here, so they report unsupported), and `engine_bench` (no bench target exists).

**Gaps and decisions to review**
- **Graphics and mesh PSOs are not built.** DX12 and Vulkan still return `Unsupported` for them. Their state needs render passes and vertex input, so I deferred them to US-032/US-033. Existing RHI comments and two GPU test names said "until US-031", and I changed those to US-032.
- **Driver PSO blobs are not used.** The cache stores compiled bytecode only.
- **Samplers** appear in reflection but are rejected by validation, because the RHI has no sampler type yet.

**Bugs found during verification**
- Passing `-MF`/`-MD` to DXC silently suppresses codegen, so the include list now comes from a second `-M` pass.
- The DXIL table parser stopped at a blank comment line, and the diagnostic parser treated source excerpts as errors.
- Windows dependency paths lost their backslashes to make-style unescaping, so the cache never stamped them.

Each of these was caught by the test suites. I also updated `progress.md` and `docs/build.md`, and set `passes: true` in `tasks/prd.json`.
